{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH2TraceForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeH2TraceForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH2Wedderburn","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Trace.Basic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.regTrace_eq_sum_characters","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.regTrace_eq_sum_characters","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH2TraceForm.lean#L94-L104","doc":"**Wedderburn reading of the regular trace.** The regular trace of\n`H₂(q)` is the sum of the two irreducible characters `χ_{l±}` for\nthe distinct roots `l±` of the Hecke quadratic — the trace-level\nshadow of the split `H₂ ≅ R × R` (`HeckeH2Wedderburn.wedderburn`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.root_sum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.root_sum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH2TraceForm.lean#L85-L92","doc":"Vieta for the Hecke quadratic: two **distinct** roots of\n`l² = h·l + 1` sum to `h`. Needs `NoZeroDivisors` — over a ring\nwith zero divisors two distinct roots need not obey Vieta. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.regTraceForm_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.regTraceForm_apply","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH2TraceForm.lean#L74-L83","doc":"**The regular trace of H₂(q).** The trace of left multiplication\nby `a·γ + b·σ` is `2a + h·b` — the `2` is `dim_R H₂ = 2`, the `h`\nis the trace of the generator `σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.basisH2_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.basisH2_one","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH2TraceForm.lean#L69-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.basisH2_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.basisH2_zero","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH2TraceForm.lean#L64-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.basisH2_repr_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.basisH2_repr_apply","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH2TraceForm.lean#L60-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.basisH2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.basisH2","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH2TraceForm.lean#L56-L58","doc":"The standard basis `{γ, σ}` of `H₂(q)` as an R-module. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.coordEquiv_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.coordEquiv_apply","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH2TraceForm.lean#L53-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.coordEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.H2A.coordEquiv","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH2TraceForm.lean#L43-L51","doc":"The coordinate linear equivalence `H₂(q) ≃ₗ (Fin 2 → R)`,\n`a·γ + b·σ ↦ ![a, b]`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}